  "note": "The GM's whole reveal picture: the session, its link generation, its reveal epoch, and one entry per slot — the table slot and one per participant (AUD-8). It rides the GM channel's snapshot frame and nothing else (threat model 8.3). An entry whose live is null is a slot the GM is entitled to see and which is empty; a table client is never given an entry for a slot it is not entitled to, which is why absence, not a marker, is how that is expressed (WT-7). THE TABLE SLOT IS ALWAYS LISTED: `nothing revealed` is the table slot, present and empty, never an absent entry, because a GM client must not read missing state as `nothing revealed` (REVEAL-13). Owner decision O-3 amends section 7.1, REVEAL-7 and NG-20: a group display is per-recipient copies of ONE disclosure, so a DOCUMENT has at most one live disclosure, every copy carries the same disclosure_id, one disclosure_id belongs to one document, and a disclosure is EITHER the table slot alone OR one or more participant slots — never both, which would make `stop all copies` ambiguous and let a private copy be mistaken for the shared one. A Stop names the document and clears every copy.",
